From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 11:23:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 39/43] minimize: panel items show their preview while the
 overflow popup is open

With the overflow popup open, hovering a window on the panel row showed
no preview; only the items in the list did, so the list had to be closed
first. The panel row now keeps its previews: the preview is a
non-grabbing popup, so it can move from a list item to a panel item (it
is recreated on the panel surface) while the list stays open. Previews
stay off while a window menu is open.

Moving the preview between the list and the panel destroys its surface
and creates a new one. The close event of the old surface could arrive
after the new open was asked for and cancel it, so no preview appeared.
A close event now only ends an open popup and leaves a pending open in
place.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

